## This app

- Code is grouped by domain, and a domain is a folder under `app/`. Its types, queries and rules sit next to its pages, with their tests.{{if not .Empty}} `app/todos/todo.go` (`package todos`) is the todo list. The home page (`app/route.go`) and the page of one todo (`app/todos/todo+/route.go`) import `{{.Module}}/app/todos`.{{else}} The home page (`app/page.tsx`) is one line, for you to replace.{{end}}
- A new domain gets a folder under `app/` and a file named after it, such as `app/notes/note.go` (`package notes`). When it has a list page and a page per item, its code goes in the list folder, not in the `name+` folder of one item.
- The root package (`package {{.Package}}`, at the module root) holds only the hooks (`hooks.go`), the options (`options.go`: `var DBPath`) and what the whole app shares (`db.go`: `var DB`, which runs `migrations/`, the tables of every domain, and `sessions.go`, which keeps sessions in the database, so a restart signs nobody out). Domains import it as `"{{.Module}}"` and write `{{.Package}}.DB`. Go refuses import cycles, so the root package cannot import a domain that uses `{{.Package}}.DB`, or a page that imports one.
- A domain may import another one that does not depend on it: if `notes` imports `tags`, directly or through other packages, `tags` cannot import `notes`. There are no `models/`, `services/` or `handlers/` packages. See `docs/start/structure.md`.
- This app wires dependencies by hand: package-level variables such as `DB`, set up in `OnStart`, not in `init()`.

## Changing tables

- Each change is a new SQL file, `migrations/<next number>_<what>.sql`, starting with `-- +goose Up`. Then `go test -run TestSchema -update` writes `schema.sql` (never edit it).
- Never edit a file that ran anywhere but on your machine: the edit never runs there. Write a new one.
- A rollback runs older releases on the same tables, so each release must run on the next one's tables: add tables, columns that are nullable or have a default, indexes. Name the columns in every `SELECT` and `INSERT`.
- Rename or drop over three releases: add the new one and write both, read it, drop the old one once no release you could roll back to uses it, in a file whose first comment says so.
- Rebuild a table only as database.md shows, or `ON DELETE CASCADE` rows go.
- Migrations finish within `deploy.start_timeout` (30s by default): see `docs/guides/database.md`.

